Figure 3 shows the long-term stability of photovoltaic parameters including PCE, \( J_{\mathrm{sc}} \), \( V_{\mathrm{oc}} \) and \( FF \) for C12-alkylacid capped \(\mathsf{C u l n S}_{2}/\mathsf{Z n S}\) QDs and fluorescent carbon electrode copolitan solar cell free of encapsulation. The optimal device maintains nearly \(100\%\) of the initial PCE under rigorous conditions including \(80\%\) relative humidity at room temperature for 80 days, \(80~^{\circ}\mathrm{C}\) for 40 days and light irradiation for 30 days. The incorporation of QDs and LPP materials into inorganic \(\mathsf{C s P b B r}_{3}\) PSC will not degrade their long-term stability, which is caused by both stabilized \(\mathsf{C s P b B r}_{3}\) lattice and protection of hydrophobic carbon electrode.In summary, we demonstrate an inorganic \(\mathsf{C s P b B r}_{3}\) PSC by using \(\mathsf{C u l n S}_{2}/\mathsf{Z n S}\) QDs layer as a hole-conductor and fluorescent carbon film as a cathode. The precise regulation of alkyl chain length of ligands attached on the QDs surface maximizes the charge carrier extraction by balancing the surface dipole induced charge coulomb repulsive force and quantum tunneling distance, while the re-absorption of unutilized incident light by \(\mathsf{C s P b B r}_{3}\) perovskite enables a wide-spectral absorption. The optimal device with C12-QDs and \(10\%\mathsf{L P P}/\) carbon electrode achieves a champion efficiency as high as \(10.85\%\). Upon persistent attacks in \(80\%\) humidity, \(80~^{\circ}\mathrm{C}\) and one sun illumination, the inorganic \(\mathsf{C s P b B r}_{3}\) solar cell shows no obvious degradation in photovoltaic performances.
In summary, we demonstrate an inorganic \(\mathsf{C s P b B r}_{3}\) PSC by using \(\mathsf{C u l n S}_{2}/\mathsf{Z n S}\) QDs layer as a hole-conductor and fluorescent carbon film as a cathode. The precise regulation of alkyl chain length of ligands attached on the QDs surface maximizes the charge carrier extraction by balancing the surface dipole induced charge coulomb repulsive force and quantum tunneling distance, while the re-absorption of unutilized incident light by \(\mathsf{C s P b B r}_{3}\) perovskite enables a wide-spectral absorption. The optimal device with C12-QDs and \(10\%\mathsf{L P P}/\) carbon electrode achieves a champion efficiency as high as \(10.85\%\) Upon persistent attacks in \(80\%\) humidity, \(80~^{\circ}\mathrm{C}\) and one sun illumination, the inorganic \(\mathsf{C s P b B r}_{3}\) solar cell shows no obvious degradation in photovoltaic performances.
